## execute_code sandbox

Write an async function body. Use `return` to return a value to the MCP caller. Globals: `klaviyo`, `shopify`, `console`. No `fetch`/`process`/`require`/`import`. Default wall-clock: 30s; opt-in via `// @timeout 2m` at the top (max 5m).

```js
// @timeout 1m
const metricId = await klaviyo.getConversionMetricId();
const lists = await klaviyo.lists.list({ 'page[size]': '100' });
return { metricId, listCount: lists.data.length };
```

All Klaviyo calls go through the host's rate limiter (10/s standard, 1/s reporting). All Shopify GraphQL calls go through Shopify's cost budget. Reporting POSTs and ShopifyQL queries are cached server-side; repeat calls within ~5–10 minutes don't re-hit the API.

If `SHOPIFY_STORE` (plus either client credentials or access token) is not set, all `shopify.*` calls throw with a configuration error. `klaviyo.*` calls still work. Check configuration availability before calling Shopify:

```js
try {
  const tz = await shopify.timezone();
} catch (e) {
  // Shopify not configured — fall back to Klaviyo-only analysis
}
```

## klaviyo.post(path, body, options?)

Generic POST. Used primarily for reporting endpoints. When `options.tier === 'reporting'`, the response is cached for 10 minutes so repeated calls (e.g. iterating an analysis) don't burn the 1/s + 2/min budget.

**Parameters**:
- `path` (string) — e.g. `'campaign-values-reports'`
- `body` (object) — JSON:API request body
- `options.tier?` (`'standard' | 'reporting'`)

```js
const metricId = await klaviyo.getConversionMetricId();
const report = await klaviyo.post('campaign-values-reports', {
  data: { type: 'campaign-values-report', attributes: {
    timeframe: { key: 'last_30_days' },
    conversion_metric_id: metricId,
    statistics: ['recipients', 'open_rate', 'conversion_value'],
  }}
}, { tier: 'reporting' });
return report.data.attributes.results;
```

## klaviyo.campaigns.list(params?)

See https://developers.klaviyo.com/en/reference/get_campaigns. Filter syntax required — at minimum a `filter` param scoping to a channel.

```js
const { data } = await klaviyo.campaigns.list({
  filter: 'equals(messages.channel,"email")',
  sort: '-send_time',
  'page[size]': '20',
  'fields[campaign]': 'name,status,send_time',
});
return data.map(c => ({ id: c.id, ...c.attributes }));
```

## klaviyo.campaigns.get(id, params?)

Fetch one campaign. Use `include=campaign-messages,tags` to pull related entities in one call.

```js
const { data, included } = await klaviyo.campaigns.get('01H...', {
  include: 'campaign-messages',
  'fields[campaign-message]': 'label,content',
});
```

## klaviyo.flows.list(params?)

See https://developers.klaviyo.com/en/reference/get_flows.

```js
const { data } = await klaviyo.flows.list({
  filter: 'equals(status,"live")',
  'page[size]': '50',
  'fields[flow]': 'name,status,trigger_type',
});
```

