## klaviyo.profiles.list(params?)

Filter required for search. Common: `filter=equals(email,"x@y.com")` or `filter=contains(email,"acme")`.

```js
const { data } = await klaviyo.profiles.list({
  filter: 'equals(email,"alice@example.com")',
  'fields[profile]': 'email,first_name,last_name,phone_number',
});
```

## klaviyo.events.list(params?)

Filter by `metric_id` to scope to one metric (e.g. Placed Order).

```js
const metricId = await klaviyo.getConversionMetricId();
const { data } = await klaviyo.events.list({
  filter: `equals(metric_id,"${metricId}")`,
  sort: '-datetime',
  'page[size]': '50',
  include: 'profile',
});
```

```js
const { data } = await klaviyo.metrics.list({
  'fields[metric]': 'name,integration',
  'page[size]': '100',
});
```

## klaviyo.reporting.campaignValues(body)

Wrapper for `POST /campaign-values-reports`. Reporting tier — rate limited at 1/s, 2/min. Results cached 10 minutes.

```js
const metricId = await klaviyo.getConversionMetricId();
const report = await klaviyo.reporting.campaignValues({
  data: { type: 'campaign-values-report', attributes: {
    timeframe: { key: 'last_30_days' },
    conversion_metric_id: metricId,
    statistics: ['recipients', 'opens', 'open_rate', 'clicks', 'click_rate', 'conversion_value', 'conversions'],
  }}
});
return report.data.attributes.results
  .sort((a, b) => b.statistics.conversion_value - a.statistics.conversion_value)
  .slice(0, 5);
```

## klaviyo.reporting.flowValues(body)

Same shape as campaignValues but for flows. `POST /flow-values-reports`.

```js
const metricId = await klaviyo.getConversionMetricId();
const report = await klaviyo.reporting.flowValues({
  data: { type: 'flow-values-report', attributes: {
    timeframe: { key: 'last_30_days' },
    conversion_metric_id: metricId,
    statistics: ['recipients', 'click_rate', 'conversion_rate', 'conversion_value'],
  }}
});
```

## shopify.gql(query, options?)

Low-level GraphQL escape hatch. Cost-budget aware: waits until enough capacity restores before sending. Auto-retries once on `THROTTLED`.

**Parameters**:
- `query` (string) — GraphQL document
- `options.variables?` (object)
- `options.estimatedCost?` (number, default 10) — used to pre-wait if budget is low

**Returns**: the `data` field of the GraphQL response.

```js
const data = await shopify.gql(`
  query($first: Int!) {
    products(first: $first, sortKey: TITLE) {
      nodes { id title vendor }
    }
  }
`, { variables: { first: 50 } });
return data.products.nodes;
```

## shopify.timezone()

Returns the store's IANA timezone string (e.g. `'America/New_York'`). Cached for server lifetime — call freely.

```js
const tz = await shopify.timezone();
const today = new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-CA', { timeZone: tz });
```

## Recipe: full DTC health dashboard

This replaces the old `dtc_dashboard` tool. Run both API surfaces in parallel via `Promise.all`.

```js
// @timeout 1m
const days = 30;
const metricId = await klaviyo.getConversionMetricId();

const [sales, campaignReport, flowReport] = await Promise.all([
  shopify.ql(`FROM sales SHOW gross_sales, net_sales, orders SINCE -${days}d UNTIL today`),
  klaviyo.reporting.campaignValues({
    data: { type: 'campaign-values-report', attributes: {
      timeframe: { key: 'last_30_days' },
      conversion_metric_id: metricId,
      statistics: ['conversion_value', 'recipients', 'open_rate'],
    }}
  }),
  klaviyo.reporting.flowValues({
    data: { type: 'flow-values-report', attributes: {
      timeframe: { key: 'last_30_days' },
      conversion_metric_id: metricId,
      statistics: ['conversion_value', 'recipients'],
    }}
  }),
]);

const row = sales.rows[0] || {};
const totalRevenue = parseFloat(row.net_sales || '0');
const orders = parseInt(row.orders || '0');

const campaignRevenue = (campaignReport.data.attributes.results || [])
  .reduce((s, r) => s + (r.statistics.conversion_value || 0), 0);
const flowRevenue = (flowReport.data.attributes.results || [])
  .reduce((s, r) => s + (r.statistics.conversion_value || 0), 0);

return {
  period_days: days,
  sales: { revenue: totalRevenue, orders, aov: orders ? totalRevenue / orders : 0 },
  email: {
    total_email_revenue: campaignRevenue + flowRevenue,
    pct_of_total: totalRevenue ? ((campaignRevenue + flowRevenue) / totalRevenue) * 100 : 0,
    campaign_revenue: campaignRevenue,
    flow_revenue: flowRevenue,
  },
};
```

```js
const metricId = await klaviyo.getConversionMetricId();
const report = await klaviyo.reporting.campaignValues({
  data: { type: 'campaign-values-report', attributes: {
    timeframe: { key: 'last_30_days' },
    conversion_metric_id: metricId,
    statistics: ['recipients', 'opens_unique', 'open_rate', 'clicks_unique', 'click_rate', 'conversion_value'],
  }}
});

const rows = (report.data.attributes.results || [])
  .map(r => ({
    campaign_id: r.groupings.campaign_id,
    recipients: r.statistics.recipients,
    open_rate: r.statistics.open_rate,
    click_rate: r.statistics.click_rate,
    revenue: r.statistics.conversion_value,
  }))
  .sort((a, b) => b.revenue - a.revenue)
  .slice(0, 10);

// Hydrate names (only for the top 10 — saves rate-limit budget)
for (const row of rows) {
  const { data } = await klaviyo.campaigns.get(row.campaign_id, {
    'fields[campaign]': 'name,send_time',
  });
  row.name = data.attributes.name;
  row.send_time = data.attributes.send_time;
}
return rows;
```
